      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, it seems your logs are from the host kernel, not from the guest kernel? (It is indicated by the following: 1. The guest usually should only print TSC frequency, not CPU frequency, since it doesn\u0027t know the CPU frequency. 2. All these 3 TSC frequency numbers divide by 38.4 MHz which indicates that they are actual precise TSC frequencies.)\n\nSo that\u0027s a different thing (and is not an issue). Yes, on modern Intel CPUs the TSC frequency doesn\u0027t match the CPU frequency (actually the CPU frequency is not constant, while the TSC frequency is), and this patch doesn\u0027t depend on the CPU frequency at all.\n\nThe TODO is about a different thing: with this patch, in a pVM you should see the TSC frequency 4-5 MHz higher than the in the host.",
