      "message": "Yeah I saw this comment and I am not worry about the  0.1-0.2% calculation error which I\u0027ve noticed, just wasn\u0027t sure if all those different detected TSC frequencies on different Intel CPUs (e.g. in example that I posted, or some other that I am not aware of) will work fine with this code and will not cause some more significant errors. There is statement in the comment that:\n\n```\n                                 * .. use 38.4 MHz\n\t\t\t\t * which is the typical TSC crystal clock frequency\n\t\t\t\t * on today\u0027s Intel\u0027s desktop CPUs.\n```\nand just trying to make sure that it is correct for CPUs that we care about and if not if we need yet another TODO?\nBut seems from examples that I used, the `Detected x MHz TSC` are clean multiple of 38.4 MHz which should be fine.\n\nDespite of above maybe s/the typical TSC crystal clock frequency/the typical crystal clock frequency/ to not mislead someone who look on the dmesg which says \"tsc: Detected 3187.200 MHz TSC\", WDYT?",
